+## Native use
+
+Use this art-direction method with the host's existing presentation authoring workflow. It adds visual-system and composition decisions; it does not select a destination, install a renderer or replace the native presentation provider. Keep required text, tables, charts and diagrams editable. Use `pptx-quality-gates` for local PPTX checks and inspect the actual rendered deck.
+
+The source's aesthetic ratios, element limits, required cover/closing elements, motif repetition and avoid lists are editorial starting points. Follow the user's brief, reference, accessibility needs, evidence and fixed slide count first. Keep an effective existing design. Choose a conclusion headline when supported; topic titles suit setup and explanation slides. Preserve neutral comparisons unless the task and evidence justify emphasis. Never imply a winner, change chart scales or crop evidence to make a claim. Functional cycles may use circular diagrams. Do not add decoration just to satisfy a motif.
+
+The complete upstream method follows. For reusable tokens, layout diagrams and tool translations, consult [the source specification](upstream/slides.md) as needed; its sample palettes and style rules are examples. The original [skill](upstream/skill/ORIGINAL-SKILL.txt), license and pinned provenance are retained. Source claims about award-winning decks and research quality are unverified. Build the requested artifact, rather than stopping at a design description.
 
